
================================================================
 ZYNQ-7000 SECURITY POSTURE   (UG585 v1.12.2 Appendix B)
 mem-AP: uscale.axi
================================================================
 devcfg: CTRL=0x0c007e87 LOCK=0x0000000f STATUS=0x4000082c MCTRL=0x3c000000
----------------------------------------------------------------
 (1) IDENTITY
   PSS_IDCODE               Zynq-7000  device=7z020 (code 0x07)  IDCODE rev=1
   Silicon version (PS_VERSION) 3.1 (code 3)
 (2) BOOT
   Boot device (BOOT_MODE)  Quad-SPI (0x1); PLL enabled; JTAG chain cascade
   Last reset cause         POR
   BootROM error code       0x0005  <- NON-ZERO (boot fault / lockdown)
 (3) SECURE BOOT & eFUSE
   Booted securely (SEC_EN) YES — this boot was authenticated/encrypted
   eFuse SECURE_EN          BLOWN — secure boot is ENFORCED in hardware (HARDENED)
   eFuse JTAG_DIS           not blown — JTAG/DAP allowed
   eFuse SW_RESERVE         BLOWN — BBRAM AES key disabled (eFuse key forced)
   Secure lockdown          clear
   DEVCI illegal-access     clear
 (4) DEBUG / DAP
   ARM DAP (DAP_EN)         ENABLED (111)
   Invasive (DBGEN)         disabled
   Non-invasive (NIDEN)     disabled
   Secure-inv (SPIDEN)      disabled
   Secure-non-inv (SPNIDEN) disabled
   JTAG scan chain          enabled
   Debug lock (LOCK.DBG)    LOCKED — CTRL(debug) frozen until POR (no register reopen)
 (5) CRYPTO
   PL AES engine (AES_EN)   ON (111)
   AES key source (FUSE)    eFuse key
   SEU lockdown (SEU_EN)    off
 (6) CONFIG LOCK & TRUSTZONE
   SLCR write-protect       LOCKED
   APU CFGSDISABLE          SET — sys-ctrl + GIC writes locked (POR-clear)
   APU CP15SDISABLE         SET — CP15 writes locked per-core (POR-clear)
   DMAC TrustZone (TZ_DMA_NS) NON-SECURE
   DMAC peripheral TZ       TZ_DMA_PERIPH_NS = 0x0 (per-channel NS bits)
----------------------------------------------------------------
 VERDICT: HARDENING PRESENT — see the ON/BLOWN/LOCKED lines + the reopen lever
